---
import LegalLayout from '../../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
---

<LegalLayout
  locale="en"
  title="Delete your Engram account"
  description="How to delete your Engram account and the data tied to it."
  effective="October 8, 2026"
  selfPath="/en/delete-account"
  altPath="/delete-account"
>
  <p class="lead">
    You can delete your Engram account at any time. Deleting it removes your
    account and the data we hold about it right away.
  </p>

  <h2>From the app</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Open Engram and tap your avatar to go to <strong>Account</strong>.</li>
    <li>Scroll to the bottom and tap <strong>Delete account</strong>.</li>
    <li>Confirm. You are signed out and the account is gone.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Without the app</h2>
  <p>
    Email <a href="mailto:support@engramcards.com?subject=Delete%20my%20account">support@engramcards.com</a>
    from the Google account you signed in with, with the subject "Delete my
    account". We delete it within 7 days and reply to confirm.
  </p>

  <h2>What is deleted</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Your account (name, email and Google account identifier).</li>
    <li>Your plan, voice-minute and AI-deck usage, and token usage counts.</li>
    <li>Feedback you sent from the app.</li>
    <li>The link between your account and your Google Play purchase.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What is not deleted</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Your Google Play subscription is not cancelled.</strong> Cancel it
      first in Google Play → Payments &amp; subscriptions → Subscriptions.
    </li>
    <li>
      Your decks stay on your phone: AnkiDroid decks are in AnkiDroid, and decks
      you made in Engram stay in the app until you uninstall it.
    </li>
    <li>
      Crash reports and analytics events are kept by Firebase Crashlytics and
      PostHog for their limited retention period, then removed.
    </li>
  </ul>
</LegalLayout>
